; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Petal, Flower, Garden
; CATEGORY: Classic Logo
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     procedures, arcs, building blocks, color
; SUMMARY:  Builds a garden the classic way: quarter circles make a petal, petals make a flower, flowers make a garden.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Draws three flowers on stems with leaves, standing on green grass.
;   Each flower has a different number of petals and a different color.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Then try  clean flower 8 5 "#ff66aa  in the command center.
;   The inputs are the number of petals, the petal size and the color.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * small procedures used as building blocks for bigger ones
;   * FILLED to color in a shape the turtle walks around
;   * the turtle ends where it started, so pieces fit together
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Give a flower 12 petals of size 2.
;   * Change QCIRCLE to turn 3 degrees 30 times. What happens to the petals?
;   * Add a fourth flower, or a sun in the sky made of petals.
; ============================================================

; Papert's book Mindstorms (1980) uses exactly this chain of ideas to
; show how a child builds big things out of small ones: a quarter
; circle, then a petal from two quarter circles, then a flower from
; petals. Each piece is easy to check on its own.

; A quarter of a circle: 18 steps of 5 degrees is 90 degrees in all.
to qcircle :size
  repeat 18 [forward :size right 5]
end

; Two quarter circles back to back make a pointed petal. After the two
; RIGHT 90s the turtle has turned 90+90+90+90 = 360, so it ends facing
; the way it started. That is what makes the next step easy.
to petal :size
  qcircle :size
  right 90
  qcircle :size
  right 90
end

to flower :petals :size :color
  setpencolor :color
  repeat :petals [
    filled :color [petal :size]
    right 360 / :petals
  ]
  ; a yellow middle, drawn as one fat dot on top of the petals
  setpensize :size * 7
  setpencolor [250 200 40]
  dot pos
  setpensize 2
end

; A leaf is a petal too, just green and lying on its side.
to leaf :size :heading
  setheading :heading
  setpencolor [40 140 60]
  filled [80 180 90] [petal :size]
end

; PLANT draws the stem from the middle of the flower down to the
; ground, with one leaf on the way, and then the flower head. Later
; drawing covers earlier drawing, so the head hides the top of the stem.
to plant :x :petals :size :color :height
  penup setxy :x :height setheading 180 pendown
  setpencolor [40 140 60]
  setpensize 4
  forward :height + 200
  back 80
  setpensize 2
  leaf 3 30
  penup setxy :x :height setheading 0 pendown
  flower :petals :size :color
end

to grass
  penup setxy -400 -200 setheading 90 pendown
  filled [110 190 90] [forward 800 right 90 forward 100 right 90 forward 800 right 90 forward 100]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [225 240 255]
setpensize 2
grass
plant -230 6 4 [230 60 90] 60
plant 0 10 3 [150 90 220] 150
plant 230 8 3.5 [255 140 40] 90
